<BRK/>
<SPT><TTL>INSTALLATION</TTL><BRK/>
<BRK/>
<TXT>Electrical installations must conform to[ <RID>IEEE C2</RID>,] <RID>NFPA 70</RID>, and to the requirements specified herein.</TXT><BRK/>
<OLG><BRK/>
<OLI>Provide chargers per manufacturer instructions and recommendations.  EVCF must be programmed and configured by a certified installer.</OLI><BRK/></OLG>
<BRK/></SPT>
[<SPT><TTL>GROUNDING</TTL><BRK/>
<NTE><BRK/>
<AST/><BRK/>
<NPR>NOTE:  Use this paragraph when a new electrical service is being created for the EVCF system.</NPR><BRK/>
<AST/><BRK/></NTE>
<BRK/>
<TXT><RID>NFPA 70</RID>, ANSI/<RID>IEEE 142</RID>[ and <RID>IEEE C2</RID>], except provide grounding systems with a resistance to solid earth ground not exceeding 5 ohms.  Complete 
ground testing at proposed EVCF location with the solid earth.</TXT><BRK/>
<BRK/>
<SPT><TTL>Grounding Electrodes</TTL><BRK/>
<BRK/>
<TXT>Provide driven ground rods as specified in Section <SRF>33 71 02</SRF> UNDERGROUND ELECTRICAL DISTRIBUTION.  Connect ground conductors to the upper end of 
ground rods by exothermic weld or compression connector.  Provide compression connectors at equipment end of ground conductors.</TXT><BRK/>
<BRK/></SPT>
</SPT>]<SPT><TTL>WIRING AND CONDUIT</TTL><BRK/>
<OLG><BRK/>
