<BRK/></SPT>
]<SPT><TTL>Performance of Acceptance Checks and Tests</TTL><BRK/>
<BRK/>
<TXT>Perform in accordance with the manufacturer's recommendations and include the following visual and mechanical inspections and electrical tests.  
Submit reports, including acceptance criteria.</TXT><BRK/>
<BRK/>
<SPT><TTL>EVCF</TTL><BRK/>
<OLG><BRK/>
<OLI>Visual and mechanical inspection.</OLI><BRK/>
<BRK/>
<OLI LEVEL="2">Compare equipment nameplate data with specifications and approved shop drawings.</OLI><BRK/>
<BRK/>
<OLI LEVEL="2">Inspect physical and mechanical condition.  Check for damage.</OLI><BRK/>
<BRK/>
<OLI LEVEL="2">Inspect anchorage, alignment, and grounding.</OLI><BRK/>
<BRK/>
<OLI LEVEL="2">Perform specific inspections and mechanical tests as recommended by manufacturer.</OLI><BRK/>
<BRK/>
<OLI>Electrical Tests</OLI><BRK/>
<BRK/>
<OLI LEVEL="2">Perform resistance measurements through all bolted connections with low-resistance ohmmeter.</OLI><BRK/>
<BRK/>
<OLI LEVEL="2">Test wiring rated 600 volt and less to verify that no short circuits or accidental grounds exist.  Perform insulation resistance 
tests on wiring No. 6 AWG and larger diameter using instrument which applies voltage of 1,000 volts DC for 600 volt rated wiring 
and 500 volts DC for 300 volt rated wiring per NETA ATS to provide direct reading of resistance.  All existing wiring to be reused 
must also be tested.</OLI><BRK/>
<BRK/>
<OLI LEVEL="2">Perform insulation-resistance test on control wiring; do not perform this test on wiring connected to solid-state components.</OLI><BRK/>
<BRK/>
<OLI LEVEL="2">Perform control wiring performance test.</OLI><BRK/>
<BRK/>
<OLI LEVEL="2">Verify voltage levels.</OLI><BRK/>
<BRK/>
<OLI LEVEL="2">Check ground fault circuit interrupt.</OLI><BRK/>
<BRK/>
<OLI LEVEL="2">Check pilot signal detection and verification.</OLI><BRK/>
<BRK/>
<OLI LEVEL="2">Verify current limit for programmable load sharing and load capping.</OLI><BRK/>
<BRK/>
<OLI LEVEL="2">Verify operation of alarms.</OLI><BRK/>
<BRK/>
<OLI LEVEL="2">Verify EVCF Electronic Data Interface.</OLI><BRK/>
<BRK/>
<OLI LEVEL="2">If the EVCF system is connected to a distribution transformer:</OLI><NED/><BRK/>
<BRK/>
<OLI LEVEL="3">Test the outgoing transformer voltage</OLI><BRK/>
<BRK/>
<OLI LEVEL="3">Test the available capacity on the transformer</OLI><BRK/>
<BRK/>
<OLI LEVEL="2">Measure duty cycle to see max current available for charging all EVCFs.</OLI><BRK/></OLG>
<BRK/>
<TXT>Values of test must be within limits of manufacturer's recommendations.</TXT><BRK/>
<BRK/></SPT>
</SPT></SPT></PRT>    <END/><BRK/></SEC>